==English==

===Etymology===
Apparently from the sound made; believed to have first appeared in comic strips.

===Noun===
A person of questionable intelligence and/or maturity living in Derry City (Northern Ireland) or its environs. Its American English equivalent would be somewhere between a 'douche' and a 'goofball'... if they even exist. It's not the end of the world to be called a gack. Some do so affectionately.

"You're such a gack hi!" /"His mucker is a total gack" / "People who talk too loud on public transport are gacks!"

===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# {{often|repeated several times}} The sound of a cat coughing up a [[hairball]].
# Also used of similar noises, particularly one made to show disgust or disapproval.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To make a 'gack' noise.
# {{transitive}} To expectorate a hairball.

